<http://data.silknow.org/object/638cd027-397a-361f-a1b0-72075aff82b7/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Girl's bonnet of undyed braided straw. This in an example of pressed 'brilliant' effect wheat straw, which is sewn by hand. The bonnet has a conical crown flaring into a slightly upturned brim. The crown is half lined with glazed cotton, and the brim is lined with pleated net over white satin.  The bonnet fastens beneath the chin with tying strings of white silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/638cd027-397a-361f-a1b0-72075aff82b7> .

